---
# Rendered through the manifests role's SECRET list (0600 + no_log), and read by the
# Deployment as HEADLAMP_CONFIG_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET when headlamp_k8s_oidc_enabled is on.
#
# Rendered even while OIDC is OFF, deliberately: an unused client secret authorises nobody,
# and it means arming the login is one variable rather than another round of SOPS work.
#
# The PLAINTEXT half of the Authelia client credential. Authelia's own config holds only the
# pbkdf2 digest (`headlamp_oidc_client_secret_hash`) — a relying party has to send the
# plaintext at the token endpoint, so the two SOPS keys are ONE credential in two forms and
# must be rotated together. Same pairing as grafana's, in claude-otel/grafana-secret.yaml.j2.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: headlamp-oidc
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
  client_secret: "{{ headlamp_oidc_client_secret }}"
